abstract: >-
  Target-bit-aware KV-cache quantization and physically packed serving for
  large language model inference. The frozen K3/V2/G32/R4/META8g64 configuration
  increases observed paged KV capacity on the evaluated H100 system, with
  higher latency and lower throughput. Canonical logical quality is
  model-dependent and is evaluated separately from physical serving.
  Apache-2.0 applies to Ryan Zhang's original software code only, subject to
  docs/LICENSING.md. Paper assets, research data, third-party materials, and
  non-code documentation are excluded from this grant; existing third-party
  licenses and notices remain in effect.
keywords:
  - "KV-cache quantization"
  - "LLM inference"
  - "memory capacity"
  - "reproducible research"
